[2026-03-14T21:17:31.851Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eGVZAsPfUNsZDXrs3xQu9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# LinearClone Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Login Page (`/login`)\n     4→\n     5→**Components**: LoginForm\n     6→\n     7→### LoginForm\n     8→\n     9→#### Test: Login form renders with email and password fields\n    10→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/login` (not authenticated)\n    11→- **Expected**: The page displays an email input field, a password input field, a \"Sign in\" button, and a \"Sign up\" link. The form has a clean, centered layout with the app branding.\n    12→\n    13→#### Test: Successful login with valid credentials\n    14→- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\" and password \"password123\"\n    15→- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks the \"Sign in\" button\n    16→- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues`. A session token is stored in localStorage. The sidebar navigation is visible.\n    17→\n    18→#### Test: Login fails with invalid email\n    19→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    20→- **Action**: User enters \"nonexistent@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    21→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page. No session token is stored.\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: Login fails with incorrect password\n    24→- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\". User is on `/login`.\n    25→- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in email, \"wrongpassword\" in password, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    26→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    27→\n    28→#### Test: Login form validates required fields\n    29→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    30→- **Action**: User clicks \"Sign in\" without entering email or password\n    31→- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for both email and password fields indicating they are required.\n    32→\n    33→#### Test: Login form validates email format\n    34→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    35→- **Action**: User enters \"notanemail\" in the email field and clicks \"Sign in\"\n    36→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n    37→\n    38→#### Test: Navigate to sign up page from login\n    39→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    40→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sign up\" link\n    41→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/signup`.\n    42→\n    43→#### Test: Password field masks input\n    44→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n    45→- **Action**: User types in the password field\n    46→- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n    47→\n    48→#### Test: Login form can be submitted via Enter key\n    49→- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`, has entered valid email and password\n    50→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field\n    51→- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Sign in\".\n    52→\n    53→#### Test: Login redirects authenticated users\n    54→- **Initial state**: User is already authenticated (valid session token in localStorage)\n    55→- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n    56→- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues` instead of seeing the login form.\n    57→\n    58→## Sign Up Page (`/signup`)\n    59→\n    60→**Components**: SignUpForm\n    61→\n    62→### SignUpForm\n    63→\n    64→#### Test: Sign up form renders with name, email, and password fields\n    65→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/signup` (not authenticated)\n    66→- **Expected**: The page displays a name input field, an email input field, a password input field, a \"Create account\" button, and a \"Log in\" link. The form has a clean, centered layout.\n    67→\n    68→#### Test: Successful account creation\n    69→- **Initial state**: No account exists for \"newuser@test.com\". User is on `/signup`.\n    70→- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"newuser@test.com\" in email, \"securepass123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n    71→- **Expected**: Account is created. A default workspace is created for the user. User is redirected to `/my-issues`. A session token is stored in localStorage.\n    72→\n    73→#### Test: Sign up fails with existing email\n    74→- **Initial state**: An account already exists with email \"existing@test.com\". User is on `/signup`.\n    75→- **Action**: User enters \"John Doe\" in name, \"existing@test.com\" in email, \"password123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n    76→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the sign up page.\n    77→\n    78→#### Test: Sign up form validates required fields\n    79→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n    80→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create account\" without filling in any fields\n    81→- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for name, email, and password fields indicating they are required.\n    82→\n    83→#### Test: Sign up form validates email format\n    84→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n    85→- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"bademail\" in email, \"password123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n    86→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n    87→\n    88→#### Test: Sign up form validates password minimum length\n    89→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n    90→- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"jane@test.com\" in email, \"abc\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n    91→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the password is too short (minimum 8 characters).\n    92→\n    93→#### Test: Navigate to login page from sign up\n    94→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n    95→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Log in\" link\n    96→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/login`.\n    97→\n    98→#### Test: Password field masks input on sign up\n    99→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n   100→- **Action**: User types in the password field\n   101→- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n   102→\n   103→#### Test: Sign up form can be submitted via Enter key\n   104→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`, has entered valid name, email, and password\n   105→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field\n   106→- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Create account\".\n   107→\n   108→#### Test: Sign up redirects authenticated users\n   109→- **Initial state**: User is already authenticated (valid session token in localStorage)\n   110→- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n   111→- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues` instead of seeing the sign up form.\n   112→\n   113→## Navigation Sidebar\n   114→\n   115→**Components**: Sidebar, SidebarCollapse, KeyboardShortcuts\n   116→\n   117→### Sidebar\n   118→\n   119→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace header\n   120→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   121→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays the workspace name at the top. The workspace name is clickable.\n   122→\n   123→#### Test: Sidebar workspace header navigates to home\n   124→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and viewing `/team/1/issues`\n   125→- **Action**: User clicks the workspace name in the sidebar header\n   126→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues` (home page).\n   127→\n   128→#### Test: Sidebar renders main navigation links\n   129→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   130→- **Expected**: The sidebar shows \"My Issues\" with a user-circle icon and \"Inbox\" with an inbox icon. Both are clickable navigation links.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Sidebar My Issues link navigates correctly\n   133→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`\n   134→- **Action**: User clicks \"My Issues\" in the sidebar\n   135→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`. The \"My Issues\" link appears selected/active with visual distinction (e.g., highlighted background).\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox link navigates correctly\n   138→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   139→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   140→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The \"Inbox\" link appears selected/active.\n   141→\n   142→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox shows unread notification count badge\n   143→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications\n   144→- **Expected**: The \"Inbox\" link in the sidebar displays a badge showing \"3\". The badge is visually distinct (e.g., accent color background).\n   145→\n   146→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge updates when notifications are read\n   147→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, badge shows \"3\"\n   148→- **Action**: User navigates to `/inbox` and marks one notification as read\n   149→- **Expected**: The badge count updates to \"2\". If all notifications are read, the badge disappears.\n   150→\n   151→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n   152→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 0 unread notifications\n   153→- **Expected**: No badge is shown next to the \"Inbox\" link.\n   154→\n   155→#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n   156→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n   157→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n   158→\n   159→#### Test: Sidebar team section is collapsible\n   160→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   161→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" team section header\n   162→- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n   163→\n   164→#### Test: Sidebar team section collapse toggles multiple times\n   165→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   166→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" header to collapse, then clicks it again to expand, then collapses it once more\n   167→- **Expected**: Each click toggles the section correctly. After three clicks the section is collapsed.\n   168→\n   169→#### Test: Sidebar team Issues link navigates to team issues page\n   170→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   171→- **Action**: User clicks \"Issues\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   172→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/issues`. The link appears selected/active.\n   173→\n   174→#### Test: Sidebar team Active Cycle link navigates to cycles page\n   175→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   176→- **Action**: User clicks \"Active Cycle\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   177→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n   180→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   181→- **Action**: User clicks \"Projects\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   182→- **Expected**: User is navigated to the projects page filtered by this team, or to `/projects` with the team filter applied.\n   183→\n   184→#### Test: Sidebar team Views link navigates to saved views\n   185→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   186→- **Action**: User clicks \"Views\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   187→- **Expected**: User is navigated to a views page for the team showing saved filtered views.\n   188→\n   189→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace section links\n   190→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   191→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n   192→\n   193→#### Test: Sidebar All Projects link navigates correctly\n   194→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   195→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Projects\" in the workspace section\n   196→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/projects`.\n   197→\n   198→#### Test: Sidebar All Teams link navigates correctly\n   199→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   200→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10e19085-a83f-4be1-bcf4-a4ad823ec258","uuid":"9153cccb-67f8-4eb3-9d65-2c6e4d152fd9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md","content":"# LinearClone Test Specification\n\n## Login Page (`/login`)\n\n**Components**: LoginForm\n\n### LoginForm\n\n#### Test: Login form renders with email and password fields\n- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/login` (not authenticated)\n- **Expected**: The page displays an email input field, a password input field, a \"Sign in\" button, and a \"Sign up\" link. The form has a clean, centered layout with the app branding.\n\n#### Test: Successful login with valid credentials\n- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\" and password \"password123\"\n- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks the \"Sign in\" button\n- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues`. A session token is stored in localStorage. The sidebar navigation is visible.\n\n#### Test: Login fails with invalid email\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n- **Action**: User enters \"nonexistent@test.com\" in the email field, \"password123\" in the password field, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page. No session token is stored.\n\n#### Test: Login fails with incorrect password\n- **Initial state**: A user account exists with email \"user@test.com\". User is on `/login`.\n- **Action**: User enters \"user@test.com\" in email, \"wrongpassword\" in password, and clicks \"Sign in\"\n- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Invalid email or password\"). The user remains on the login page.\n\n#### Test: Login form validates required fields\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Sign in\" without entering email or password\n- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for both email and password fields indicating they are required.\n\n#### Test: Login form validates email format\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n- **Action**: User enters \"notanemail\" in the email field and clicks \"Sign in\"\n- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n\n#### Test: Navigate to sign up page from login\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sign up\" link\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/signup`.\n\n#### Test: Password field masks input\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`\n- **Action**: User types in the password field\n- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n\n#### Test: Login form can be submitted via Enter key\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/login`, has entered valid email and password\n- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field\n- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Sign in\".\n\n#### Test: Login redirects authenticated users\n- **Initial state**: User is already authenticated (valid session token in localStorage)\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues` instead of seeing the login form.\n\n## Sign Up Page (`/signup`)\n\n**Components**: SignUpForm\n\n### SignUpForm\n\n#### Test: Sign up form renders with name, email, and password fields\n- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/signup` (not authenticated)\n- **Expected**: The page displays a name input field, an email input field, a password input field, a \"Create account\" button, and a \"Log in\" link. The form has a clean, centered layout.\n\n#### Test: Successful account creation\n- **Initial state**: No account exists for \"newuser@test.com\". User is on `/signup`.\n- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"newuser@test.com\" in email, \"securepass123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n- **Expected**: Account is created. A default workspace is created for the user. User is redirected to `/my-issues`. A session token is stored in localStorage.\n\n#### Test: Sign up fails with existing email\n- **Initial state**: An account already exists with email \"existing@test.com\". User is on `/signup`.\n- **Action**: User enters \"John Doe\" in name, \"existing@test.com\" in email, \"password123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the sign up page.\n\n#### Test: Sign up form validates required fields\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Create account\" without filling in any fields\n- **Expected**: Validation errors are shown for name, email, and password fields indicating they are required.\n\n#### Test: Sign up form validates email format\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"bademail\" in email, \"password123\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the email format is invalid.\n\n#### Test: Sign up form validates password minimum length\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n- **Action**: User enters \"Jane Doe\" in name, \"jane@test.com\" in email, \"abc\" in password, and clicks \"Create account\"\n- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the password is too short (minimum 8 characters).\n\n#### Test: Navigate to login page from sign up\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Log in\" link\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/login`.\n\n#### Test: Password field masks input on sign up\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`\n- **Action**: User types in the password field\n- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n\n#### Test: Sign up form can be submitted via Enter key\n- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`, has entered valid name, email, and password\n- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field\n- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Create account\".\n\n#### Test: Sign up redirects authenticated users\n- **Initial state**: User is already authenticated (valid session token in localStorage)\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues` instead of seeing the sign up form.\n\n## Navigation Sidebar\n\n**Components**: Sidebar, SidebarCollapse, KeyboardShortcuts\n\n### Sidebar\n\n#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace header\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n- **Expected**: The sidebar displays the workspace name at the top. The workspace name is clickable.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar workspace header navigates to home\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and viewing `/team/1/issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks the workspace name in the sidebar header\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues` (home page).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar renders main navigation links\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n- **Expected**: The sidebar shows \"My Issues\" with a user-circle icon and \"Inbox\" with an inbox icon. Both are clickable navigation links.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar My Issues link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"My Issues\" in the sidebar\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`. The \"My Issues\" link appears selected/active with visual distinction (e.g., highlighted background).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Inbox link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The \"Inbox\" link appears selected/active.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Inbox shows unread notification count badge\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications\n- **Expected**: The \"Inbox\" link in the sidebar displays a badge showing \"3\". The badge is visually distinct (e.g., accent color background).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge updates when notifications are read\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, badge shows \"3\"\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/inbox` and marks one notification as read\n- **Expected**: The badge count updates to \"2\". If all notifications are read, the badge disappears.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 0 unread notifications\n- **Expected**: No badge is shown next to the \"Inbox\" link.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team section is collapsible\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" team section header\n- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team section collapse toggles multiple times\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" header to collapse, then clicks it again to expand, then collapses it once more\n- **Expected**: Each click toggles the section correctly. After three clicks the section is collapsed.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team Issues link navigates to team issues page\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Issues\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/issues`. The link appears selected/active.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team Active Cycle link navigates to cycles page\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Active Cycle\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Projects\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to the projects page filtered by this team, or to `/projects` with the team filter applied.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team Views link navigates to saved views\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Views\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to a views page for the team showing saved filtered views.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace section links\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar All Projects link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"All Projects\" in the workspace section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/projects`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar All Teams link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2686}}}
